        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Disabling *all* modules is done in a similar fashion: set corresponding global or local variable `mini***_disable` to `true` ([here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/89c77d220f546782f1da12fe451c6a56c479ffd4/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L58-L64) is documentation for 'mini.indentscope'). To do this automatically, create autocommand that suits your need. [Here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini.txt#L174) are approaches for some common tasks.\r\n\r\nSo in your case, adding something like this (or similar Lua API alternative) in your Neovim config should do the trick:\r\n```lua\r\nvim.cmd('au FileType neo-tree lua vim.b.miniindentscope_disable = true')\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2022-10-13T13:19:15Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/144#issuecomment-1277598579",
